{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% block main %}
<h1>Data downloads</h1>
<p class="lede">Every shown fact, with its source, as files: so this site is not the only copy. The files carry what the pages show, and none of the program's raw reading of names, vote wording or motion sentences.</p>
{% if site.export_omitted %}
<p>The data files are left out of this preview copy of the site, which is limited in size. The full site carries them.</p>
{% else %}
<p class="unofficial-intro"><strong>{{ site.unofficial.tag }}.</strong> {{ site.unofficial.notice }} Every download carries this notice in <a href="{{ root }}data/README.txt">README.txt</a>.</p>
{% for g in groups %}
{% if groups | length > 1 %}<h2>{{ g.heading }}</h2>{% endif %}
<ul class="data-files">
{% for f in g.files %}
  <li><a href="{{ root }}data/{{ f.name }}">{{ f.name }}</a>: {{ f.about }}</li>
{% endfor %}
</ul>
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
<p>Every row names the document that prints it (source_url, page) and when it was fetched. A value held back as "Not confirmed" is empty in these files, with the check that held it.</p>
<p>A text cell that would begin with =, +, - or @ (or a tab or carriage return) starts with an apostrophe, so a spreadsheet shows it as text; number columns are left as they are.</p>
{% endblock %}
